From 02e8b6ae1d153dc095c3ca4c1fa463892aabb64b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael John <mj@tierone.software>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 16:09:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] patch: fix multiple parser memory-safety bugs found by
 fuzzing

- my_exit(): guard unlink() against unallocated temp names (early exit)
- pch.c: cap all four hunkmax grow sites at MAXHUNKSIZE (an 89-byte
  patch claiming a ~4e17-line hunk drove the real binary to 16GB RSS)
- pch.c: guard p_char[p_end - 1] with p_end > 0 (OOB read)
- pch.c: guard remove_special_line rewrites against empty lines
  (p_len underflow -> OOB write, six sites) and i > 0
- pch.c: set p_len for hunk header lines (stale length -> OOB write)
- pch.c: calloc p_line and zero the grown half; NULL entries after free
- pch.c: compile with -fwrapv (line-number arithmetic relies on wrap)
- add pch_reset() and close_patch_file() for reentrant use (fuzzing)
---
 src.freebsd/patch/meson.build |  2 +
 src.freebsd/patch/pch.c       | 74 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 src.freebsd/patch/pch.h       |  2 +
 src.freebsd/patch/util.c      | 11 ++++--
 4 files changed, 73 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

